<title>SPAIN: Spanish bond market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Spanish bond market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's bond market was closed on Friday for Assumption Day national holiday and will re-open as normal on Monday.</p>
<p>Closing levels for Thursday were as follows: * 10-yr 7.35 pct T-bond 107.18 vs 106.85, yield 6.32 vs 6.36 * Sept bond future 116.83 vs 116.45 at Wednesday's close * Peseta/mark 84.52/53 vs 84.51/52</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
